    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0560" n="464" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg464"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Baron de Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I duly received your telegram this
                    morning. Of course you understand that, in the actual status of the matter and
                    in the absence of Federal jurisdiction over an offense committed in a State, the
                    agent whom we are to send to Tallulah can not assert any part in the local
                    administration of justice, but is sent to collect information for the
                    Department’s consideration and such action thereon as may be in order. His
                    functions will be the same as that of Mr. W. H. Phillips, who, as you remember,
                    was sent to Hahnville a few years ago under somewhat similar circumstances.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
